# Check text files out with LF on every platform. Windows runners default to
# core.autocrlf=true, and a CRLF shebang ("#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n") in a script that
# Vitest's globalSetup imports is not stripped by Vite's /^#!.*\n/ (`.` doesn't match
# \r), so the module fails to parse and the whole run dies before collecting a test.
* text=auto eol=lf

# An eval fixture whose bug IS its line endings: a spreadsheet export with CRLF and a byte
# order mark. Normalizing it to LF would make the task pass before the agent touches it.
src/main/agent/evals/tasks/crlf-sales-report/repo/data/sales-2026-09.csv -text
src/main/agent/evals/tasks/crlf-sales-report/repo/data/sales-2026-10.csv -text
